INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0001','A quieter morning','The morning light came through the kitchen window. Maya put a cup beside her notebook. She wrote down three small things to do. The first was to water the plants. Then she opened the door and stepped outside. A short walk helped her feel ready for the day. She did not need to rush. There was time to notice the birds and the cool air.','easy','Everyday English','65','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0002','Building something useful','A small team built a tool to help people share books. They started with a sketch on a piece of paper. Each person tested the first version with a friend. One reader could not find the search button. The team moved it closer to the top of the page. Simple changes made the tool easier to use. Good design began with listening to the people who needed it.','easy','Technology','68','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0003','The garden after rain','Rain left little drops on the green leaves. The garden smelled fresh and cool. A bird landed near the old clay pot. Lina watched it pick a seed from the ground. She filled the water bowl and placed it in the shade. The sun came out slowly. By noon the path was dry again. Even a small garden could become a home for many living things.','easy','Nature','66','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0004','The last stop','The bus stopped beside a quiet market. Sam checked his bag and looked at the map. He had never been to this town before. A shop owner showed him the way to the river. The path went past a row of bright blue doors. At the bridge he stopped to take a photo. Getting there took longer than he expected. The walk itself became the best part of the trip.','easy','Travel','70','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0005','A question worth asking','The class placed two pots near a window. One pot received water every morning. The other received water only twice a week. Each student wrote down what they saw. After seven days the leaves looked different. They compared the notes before making a claim. A useful experiment needs a clear question. It also needs a fair way to test the answer.','easy','Science','61','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0006','Learning in small steps','Noor wanted to learn a new skill. At first the task seemed too large. Her teacher asked her to work for ten minutes each day. She chose one small goal for each lesson. Some days were harder than others. She kept a record of what went well. After a month she could see real progress. Small steps had given her the confidence to keep going.','easy','Education','65','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0007','One more lap','The runners met at the park before work. They began with a slow walk around the field. Ari wanted to run faster than last week. His coach asked him to keep a steady pace first. On the final lap he still had energy to spare. He crossed the line with a smile. Training was not only about speed. Rest and good habits helped him improve too.','easy','Sports','66','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0008','The corner repair shop','A little repair shop stood beside the bakery. The owner knew most of the people who came in. He wrote every job in a plain paper book. One week he noticed that many repairs took longer than planned. He began to check each item before giving a price. Customers liked the clear advice. Careful records helped him make better choices. Trust was the most useful thing his shop could earn.','easy','Business','70','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0009','A book with a folded page','Ria found an old book on the bottom shelf. A small note was tucked between two pages. It asked the next reader to share a favorite line. She read the story on the train home. The main character made a choice she did not expect. At the end she understood the note. A story could mean something different to each reader. She added her own line and returned the book.','easy','Literature','70','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0010','The map in the archive','An old map showed a road that no longer existed. A researcher compared it with photos of the same place. She found a market where a station now stood. Some street names had changed over time. Others had remained almost the same. She checked a second source before writing her report. A single record could raise a question. Several careful records could help explain what had happened.','easy','History','67','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0011','A plan for small savings','Ben put a few coins in a jar each Friday. He wanted to buy a better desk lamp. He wrote the price on a card and kept it nearby. When he bought a snack he noted the cost. The record helped him see where his money went. He did not stop buying things he enjoyed. Instead he chose what mattered most. A clear goal made the small choices easier.','easy','Finance','69','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0012','Room to think','The room was loud when Eva tried to work. Her phone lit up every few minutes. She moved to a quiet table and put the phone away. At first her mind still wandered. She took a short break and then tried again. This time she finished one task before opening another. Attention was easier to manage when she changed her surroundings. She kept the new habit for the rest of the week.','easy','Psychology','72','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0013','A better handle','The old water jug was hard to lift. A designer watched how people used it. Some held it with both hands. Others spilled water while trying to pour. She made a new handle from thick card. People tried the model and suggested changes. The final shape was easier to grip. The best idea had come from observing a small everyday problem.','easy','Innovation','61','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0014','A clearer message','The first message was long and hard to follow. It listed five problems but did not ask a clear question. Omar read it once more before sending it. He put the main request in the first line. Then he added the details that the reader needed. He ended with a date for the next step. A short message could still be polite. Clear writing respected the time of everyone involved.','easy','Professional Communication','70','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0015','The blue envelope','A blue envelope lay under the front door. There was no name on the outside. Inside was a drawing of the street and a small red cross. Mina recognized the old tree near the corner. She walked there after lunch and found a wooden box. It held the photos her neighbor thought were lost. A note asked her to bring them home. She knocked on the next door with a smile.','easy','Storytelling','71','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0016','Watching the night sky','The town lights faded behind the hill. Above the field the sky seemed full of stars. Leo set a small telescope on the ground. His aunt showed him how to find a bright planet. They took turns looking through the lens. The air grew cold but neither wanted to leave. A simple guide helped them name a few patterns. There was still much more to learn.','easy','General Knowledge','66','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0017','Checking an explanation','A student read two reports about the same question. Both used clear charts but reached different answers. She looked at how the data had been collected. One report studied a much smaller group. The other left out an important detail. She wrote a list of strengths and limits for each. A confident claim was not always a strong claim. Evidence needed careful reading before it could support a conclusion.','easy','Academic English','69','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0018','The note on the desk','The note said, "Please bring a pen, a notebook, and your ticket." Jack checked his bag twice. Had he remembered everything? His sister called from the door: "We leave at nine!" The clock showed eight forty. He found the ticket inside a book. It was not lost after all. A few clear marks had made the short message easy to understand.','easy','Punctuation','61','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0019','A small market receipt','The shop opened at 8:30 and closed at 6:00. A notebook cost $4.50. Two pens cost $1.20 each. The clerk added the prices and checked the total. A sign offered 10% off selected items. Nia read the receipt before she left. She put the change in a small pocket. Keeping track of numbers helped her stay within the budget for the day.','easy','Numbers and Symbols','62','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-0-0020','The patient craft','The craft worker chose a smooth piece of wood. He marked a line and checked it twice. A small error at the start could affect the whole shape. He worked slowly around the curved edge. Then he set the tool down and looked again. The finished object seemed simple. Its balance came from many careful choices. Skill often grew from patience rather than from a wish to finish first.','easy','Advanced Vocabulary','69','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-1-0001','A quieter morning','The morning light came through the kitchen window. Maya put a cup beside her notebook. She wrote down three small things to do. The first was to water the plants. Then she opened the door and stepped outside. A short walk helped her feel ready for the day. She did not need to rush. There was time to notice the birds and the cool air. Looking more closely revealed why the first approach had been difficult. The people involved had different expectations, and those expectations had not been discussed at the beginning. Once the purpose was clear, it became possible to compare a few practical alternatives.','medium','Everyday English','106','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-1-0002','Building something useful','A small team built a tool to help people share books. They started with a sketch on a piece of paper. Each person tested the first version with a friend. One reader could not find the search button. The team moved it closer to the top of the page. Simple changes made the tool easier to use. Good design began with listening to the people who needed it. The next step was to keep a short record of the process. Instead of relying on a single impression, the group returned to the same question several times. This made gradual changes easier to notice and helped prevent an early assumption from becoming a final answer.','medium','Technology','114','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO passages (id,title,text,difficulty,category,words,status,created,updated,provenance) VALUES ('KD-1-0003','The garden after rain','Rain left little drops on the green leaves. The garden smelled fresh and cool. A bird landed near the old clay pot. Lina watched it pick a seed from the ground. She filled the water bowl and placed it in the shade. The sun came out slowly. By noon the path was dry again. Even a small garden could become a home for many living things. Not every attempt worked as expected. One small adjustment solved a problem while creating another, so the process required attention and patience. The useful lesson was to describe what actually happened rather than what everyone had hoped would happen.','medium','Nature','105','published','1793536902046','1793536902046','Original Keyderby editorial seed; authored for typing practice.');
